	"department": "RUSSN",
	"description": [
		"Ukrainian writer Nikolay Gogol is often miscategorized as a \"Great Russian Writer.\" Many readers are unaware that Gogol was Ukrainian and that he aimed to promote the idea of an independent Ukrainian nation. This course will critically examine the Russocentric view of Gogol and Russophone literature (literature written in Russian by non-Russian writers) by placing Gogol in the space of empire, between Russia and Ukraine. No knowledge of Russian or previous background required. Offered periodically during fall semester."
	],
